Falsifies `jh7110_entropy::verification::neither_bit_set_is_always_not_ready`.

The defect: `generation_outcome` treats `SEED_DONE` as a second reason to read the register file, so a core
that has finished seeding but has produced nothing yet is read as `Ready` and yields whatever the
`RAND` registers last held.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(generation_outcome(stat, istat, rand), GenerationOutcome::NotReady)`: `SEED_DONE` alone now
produces `Ready`.

diff --git a/crates/jh7110_entropy/src/lib.rs b/crates/jh7110_entropy/src/lib.rs
index b647a51d9..de09873d2 100644
--- a/crates/jh7110_entropy/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/jh7110_entropy/src/lib.rs
@@ -607,3 +607,3 @@ pub fn generation_outcome(stat: u32, istat: u32, rand: [u32; 8]) -> GenerationOutcome {
         GenerationOutcome::Unseeded
-    } else if istat & ISTAT_RAND_RDY != 0 {
+    } else if istat & (ISTAT_RAND_RDY | ISTAT_SEED_DONE) != 0 {
         GenerationOutcome::Ready(output_bytes(rand))
